        "text": "The email address printed on your official site sits on a domain that expires on 2026-12-04. When it lapses, mail from clients, banks and tender panels to that address stops.",
        "cites": ["f1"]
      },
      {
        "text": "That is one of several things the public internet says about Eternalgy today. Your head office phone differs across 3 sources, two email addresses are published as yours, and both your domains let anyone send mail in your name.",
        "cites": ["c1", "c2", "f2"]
      },
      {
        "text": "Your 4.7 rating from 32 reviews is a real asset. The unanswered reviews beside it work against you.",
        "cites": ["f11", "f4"]
      }
    ]
  },
  "titles": [
    {
      "id": "f1",
      "text": "The domain behind the email address on your site is nearing expiry, and your mail stops with it."
    },
    {
      "id": "f2",
      "text": "Anyone can send email as your domains, so a forged invoice can carry your name."
    },
    {
      "id": "f3",
      "text": "Your LinkedIn phone field holds a cut-off registration number, so no one can call you from it."
    },
    {
      "id": "f4",
      "text": "Your newest Google reviews, including your only low rating, have no reply from you."
    },
    {
      "id": "f5",
      "text": "Google's own check fails on the file that tells search engines how to crawl your site, which limits indexing."
    },
    {
      "id": "f6",
      "text": "Your site sends none of the standard security headers, and a bank's IT reviewer notices."
    },
    {
      "id": "f7",
      "text": "The pages search engines read link to no Contact or Privacy page, and buyers look for both."
    },
    {
      "id": "f8",
      "text": "Your about page carries no company markup, so search and AI engines cannot tie the brand to your business."
    },
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "text": "Your head office phone differs across 3 sources, so buyers may call a line you no longer answer."
    },
    {
      "id": "c2",
      "text": "Two different email addresses are published as yours, so enquiries split and letters go unanswered."
    },
    {
      "id": "c3",
      "text": "Your office list differs between your own sites, so a local customer cannot tell whether you have a branch there."
    },
    {
      "id": "c4",
      "text": "Your staff count on your own site differs from your LinkedIn page, and a tender panel sizes you by both."
    },
    {
      "id": "c5",
      "text": "Your completed project figures disagree across listings, and a buyer who sees the gap discounts all of them."
    },
    {
      "id": "c6",
      "text": "One job board lists your company under a different legal form, which can stall a vendor registration."
    },
    {
      "id": "c7",
      "text": "Your head office address differs across 4 sources, so couriers and tender checks cannot confirm it."
    },
    {
      "id": "n1",
      "text": "Reviewers share names with your staff and a listed sales contact — worth checking how that reads to a buyer."
    },
    {
      "id": "n2",
      "text": "Several 5★ reviews arrived on the same day — worth checking how that pattern reads to a sceptical buyer."
    },
    {
      "id": "n3",
      "text": "Two automated tools disagree about whether your site's crawl file works — worth checking what Google actually receives."
    },
    {
      "id": "n4",
      "text": "Several domains are in circulation for your company, which may split your brand and search signals."
    },
    {
      "id": "n5",
      "text": "Your partner and tier claims rest on your own text — worth checking that no outside page confirms them."
    },
    {
      "id": "n6",
      "text": "Your revenue claim has no outside counterpart — worth checking how it reads beside a published sales figure."
    },
    {
      "id": "n7",
      "text": "A directory's performance figures look like an older snapshot of yours — worth checking which number a buyer finds first."
    }
  ],
  "proof": {
    "id": "f1",
    "why": "The owner can confirm the registration date in a minute with a public lookup, mail stops the moment it lapses, and renewing it still leaves the forged-mail, phone and review problems untouched."
  }
}

